# CITATION file for the Classical Traffic Signal Coordination project.
# If you prefer a specific citation format not listed here, adapt from BibTeX.
title: "Classical AI-Based Traffic Signal Coordination"
abstract: >-
  An educational decision-support system that coordinates signal offsets along an
  arterial corridor. It compares an uncoordinated timing baseline, a greedy one-way
  progression baseline, and a constraint-satisfaction optimization approach using
  backtracking search, forward checking, and branch-and-bound. All plans are
  evaluated with a deterministic corridor simulation measuring vehicle waiting time,
  stops, search effort (nodes, backtracks, forward-check reductions), and runtime.
authors:
